@startuml 05_class_commands
!include _style.puml
title Undo / redo - Command pattern - crate ascii_core::history

package "ascii_core::history" {

  interface Command <<trait>> {
    + label() -> &str
    + apply(project: &mut Project)
    + revert(project: &mut Project)
  }

  class History <<struct>> {
    - undo_stack: Vec<Box<dyn Command>>
    - redo_stack: Vec<Box<dyn Command>>
    - limit: usize = 200
    - clean_marker: Option<usize>
    + new() -> History
    + execute(cmd: Box<dyn Command>, project: &mut Project)
    + record_applied(cmd: Box<dyn Command>)
    + undo(project: &mut Project) -> Option<String>
    + redo(project: &mut Project) -> Option<String>
    + can_undo() -> bool
    + can_redo() -> bool
    + undo_label() -> Option< &str >
    + redo_label() -> Option< &str >
    + mark_clean()
    + is_dirty() -> bool
  }

  class CellChange <<struct, Copy>> {
    + coord: CellCoord
    + before: Cell
    + after: Cell
  }

  class CellPatchCommand <<struct>> {
    + frame_id: FrameId
    + changes: Vec<CellChange>
    + label: String
  }

  class SetFrameBackgroundCommand <<struct>> {
    + frame_id: FrameId
    + before: Rgb
    + after: Rgb
    + {static} new(project: &Project, frame_id: FrameId, after: Rgb) -> Option<SetFrameBackgroundCommand>
  }

  class AddFrameCommand <<struct>> {
    + index: usize
    + frame: Frame
    + selected_before: usize
    + {static} blank_after(project: &mut Project, index: usize) -> AddFrameCommand
    + {static} duplicate(project: &mut Project, index: usize) -> AddFrameCommand
  }

  class DeleteFrameCommand <<struct>> {
    + index: usize
    + frame: Frame
    + selected_before: usize
    + {static} new(project: &Project, index: usize) -> Result<DeleteFrameCommand, DomainError>
  }

  class MoveFrameCommand <<struct>> {
    + from: usize
    + to: usize
    + selected_before: usize
  }

  class SetPlaybackSettingsCommand <<struct>> {
    + before_fps: Fps
    + after_fps: Fps
    + before_looping: bool
    + after_looping: bool
  }

  class CompositeCommand <<struct>> {
    + label: String
    + children: Vec<Box<dyn Command>>
  }
}

Command <|.. CellPatchCommand
Command <|.. SetFrameBackgroundCommand
Command <|.. AddFrameCommand
Command <|.. DeleteFrameCommand
Command <|.. MoveFrameCommand
Command <|.. SetPlaybackSettingsCommand
Command <|.. CompositeCommand

History o-- "0..200" Command : undo_stack
History o-- "0..*" Command : redo_stack
CompositeCommand *-- "1..*" Command : children
CellPatchCommand *-- "1..*" CellChange
CellPatchCommand ..> Project : mutates
SetFrameBackgroundCommand ..> Project : mutates
AddFrameCommand ..> Project : mutates
DeleteFrameCommand ..> Project : mutates
MoveFrameCommand ..> Project : mutates
SetPlaybackSettingsCommand ..> Project : mutates

note as N1
  Contract
  - apply() is only ever called when the project is in the exact state the command was created against
    (History guarantees this by strict LIFO order), so apply()/revert() never need to validate or fail.
  - apply() followed by revert() restores the project bit-for-bit (except Frame.revision, which only increases).
  - Commands own all data they need (they never keep references into the project).
  - Commands never touch Selection, Viewport, Brush or the file on disk.
end note

note as N2
  Rules
  - execute(cmd): cmd.apply(project); then record_applied(cmd).
  - record_applied(cmd): used when the change is already in the project (strokes, typing).
      1. redo_stack.clear()  - if clean_marker is Some(m) with m > undo_stack.len(), set clean_marker = None.
      2. undo_stack.push(cmd)
      3. if undo_stack.len() > limit: undo_stack.remove(0); clean_marker = clean_marker.and_then(|m| m.checked_sub(1))
         (a marker that falls off the bottom becomes None = "always dirty").
  - undo(): pop undo_stack, cmd.revert(project), push onto redo_stack, return Some(cmd.label()). None if empty.
  - redo(): pop redo_stack, cmd.apply(project), push onto undo_stack, return Some(label). None if empty.
  - mark_clean(): clean_marker = Some(undo_stack.len())   (called right after a successful save of the .aspr).
  - is_dirty(): clean_marker != Some(undo_stack.len())    (a brand-new project starts with clean_marker = Some(0)).
  - EditorSession::undo()/redo() always dispatches ToolEvent::Cancel to the active tool FIRST, so a running stroke / typing
    session is committed (or a drag / polygon preview discarded) before the history is touched.
end note

note as N3
  apply : idx = timeline.index_of(frame_id).unwrap(); for ch in changes (in order) frame.set_cell(ch.coord, ch.after);
          then timeline.select(idx) so the user always SEES what was changed.
  revert: same loop in REVERSE order writing ch.before; then timeline.select(idx).
  Used by: Edit text, Clear cells, Paint cells, Fill cells, "Delete selection contents".
end note

note as N4
  new(): returns None when the frame does not exist or its background already equals `after` (nothing to record).
  apply : frame.set_background(after)    revert: frame.set_background(before)
  "Apply to all frames" in the colour dialog = CompositeCommand("Set background (all frames)") containing one
  SetFrameBackgroundCommand per frame whose colour differs, so one Ctrl+Z restores every frame.
end note

note as N5
  blank_after(project, i): frame = Frame::blank(project.alloc_frame_id(), canvas, background of frame i); index = i + 1.
  duplicate(project, i) : frame = frame[i].duplicate_as(project.alloc_frame_id());  index = i + 1.
  selected_before = timeline.selected_index() at creation time.
  apply : timeline.insert(index, frame.clone()); timeline.select(index)
  revert: timeline.remove(index); timeline.select(min(selected_before, len - 1))
end note

note as N6
  new() fails with CannotRemoveLastFrame when timeline.len() == 1 (the Delete button is also disabled then).
  apply : timeline.remove(index); timeline.select(min(index, len - 1))
  revert: timeline.insert(index, frame.clone()); timeline.select(selected_before)
end note

note as N7
  Created by drag-and-drop in the frame list (from = dragged index, to = index after removal, see Timeline::move_frame).
  Not created when from == to.
  apply : timeline.move_frame(from, to); timeline.select(to)
  revert: timeline.move_frame(to, from); timeline.select(selected_before)
end note

note as N8
  Created when the FPS field or the Loop checkbox changes (one command per committed edit: Enter / focus loss / drag release
  for FPS, one click for Loop - not one per keystroke). Not created when nothing differs.
  apply : timeline.fps = after_fps; timeline.looping = after_looping
  revert: timeline.fps = before_fps; timeline.looping = before_looping
end note


